Dirty Bomb is a class-based multiplayer first person shooter developed by the guys and gals at Splash Damage.
The Good:
-it is free;
-it has a wide range of characters with their own personalities;
-it brings up an intriguing character loadout system (you have to create a squad of three different characters to bring into the matches);
-character customisation, in the sense that you can equip a loadout card for each character, which can come with up to 3 perks and a slight difference in the weapons.
The Bad
-very slow progression. The character prices, at least at the moment this review has been written, range between 30.000 and 40.000 in-game credits.
-ocassional performance hiccups, which are excusable because the game is still in beta, but I needed to bring it up for the sake of a complete review.
All in all, Dirty Bomb is a robust first person shooter and I urge you to give it a try.

